kunzite: Adreno 710 step 22, a picture drawn by the GPU on the panel (kgpu=22; the port map's 22).
hk's redwood step 22 (three 2D solid fills, then the framebuffer shows the result), redone for
a7xx after Mesa's fd6_blitter.cc (fd6_clear_surface, emit_blit_setup, emit_blit_fini with CHIP =
A7XX) and Linux's registers/adreno/a6xx.xml + adreno_pm4.xml (copies of both, and of the Mesa
sources used, in the main repo's temp/gpu-plan-review/regdb-2026-10-24): a 1080x2400 picture of
ours (rows of 4352 bytes) mapped for the GPU at 0xe0200000 (5 more tables: the pool grows to 16),
TLBIASID + sync on context 0. Command stream (type4/type7 packets built with
pm4_calc_odd_parity_bit): CP_EVENT_WRITE7 CCU_INVALIDATE_COLOR; CP_SET_MARKER RM6_BLIT2DSCALE;
RB_CCU_CACHE_CNTL 0x20000000 (sysmem: 1 CCU, depth cache 256K at 0, colour at 256K, both full);
per band RB/GRAS_A2D_BLT_CNTL 0x00f03080 (solid, FMT6_8_8_8_8_UNORM, mask 0xf, R2D_UNORM8),
TPL1_A2D_BLT_CNTL 0x20000000 (a7xx), SP_A2D_OUTPUT_INFO 0xf180 at its a7xx offset 0xa9bf,
RB_A2D_PIXEL_CNTL 0, the TPL1 source and GRAS source registers zeroed, RB_A2D_CLEAR_COLOR_DW0-3
= R, G, B, 255, RB_A2D_DEST_BUFFER_INFO 0x430 (8888, linear, WXYZ: blue first), BASE, PITCH
4352/64, GRAS_A2D_DEST_TL/BR, CP_EVENT_WRITE7 DEBUG_LABEL, CP_BLIT BLIT_OP_SCALE; three bands
(orange 0-800, white 800-1600, blue 1600-2400, hk's); then CCU_CLEAN_COLOR, CACHE_CLEAN,
CP_WAIT_FOR_IDLE and a CP_MEM_WRITE marker 0x6b677022 (scratch +0x104) + CP_WAIT_MEM_WRITES,
submitted with step 21's helper (now printing the running step). Checked from our side: the
marker, three named pixels, and every 50th row at 3 columns against its band's colour. Then the
picture is copied row by row (4320 bytes of each 4352) into the panel memory 0xb8000000 (the ABL
splash buffer that AppleCLCD presents into and the display controller scans out; an unmappable
write-combining alias, unmapped after), again every 250 ms for 15 s since iOS's presenter draws
there too. Undo: the picture's memory freed; the panel keeps it until iOS draws again.

